{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat ../research.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"audit_spec_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-04_18-11-07-dragonboat_raft-real-run/audit-spec/v3.json\",\n  \"audit_spec_version\": 3,\n  \"activity_roles\": {\n    \"A1\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Qualified support for decision formation and legal advancement\"\n    },\n    \"A2\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Context validity and acquisition, transfer or loss of authority\"\n    },\n    \"A3\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Recovery and resynchronization of eligible participation\"\n    },\n    \"A4\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Configuration and participant eligibility\"\n    },\n    \"A5\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Decision application and consumption\"\n    },\n    \"A6\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"History, persistence and reconstruction of support\"\n    },\n    \"A7\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Client contracts, invocation intervals and observed completion\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"activity_focus\": [],\n  \"understanding_status\": \"usable\",\n  \"core_overview\": {\n    \"formation\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Node/Peer proposals reach the leader, which appends current-term entries and sends predecessor-qualified replication. Followers reject mismatching prefixes or append matching entries, protect committed history and acknowledge accepted indexes. Engine persists ordinary responses before sending them (replication requests may precede persistence). Leader aggregates full-member and witness match values, selects the quorum index and commits only a current-term entry there, thereby carrying its prefix. Commit is propagated in replication/heartbeat messages; committed entries pass through a separate RSM queue to membership/application processing and client callbacks. Rejections retry with lower next; compacted histories use snapshots for active peers.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-formation\",\n        \"B-persistence\",\n        \"B-apply\",\n        \"B-recovery\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-committed\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-formation\",\n        \"S-log\",\n        \"S-replication-send\",\n        \"S-replication-recv\",\n        \"S-engine-order\",\n        \"S-node-effects\",\n        \"S-rsm-apply\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Election ticks on eligible full members trigger term increment and self-vote. Vote grants require vote eligibility and log freshness; known response admission and unique sender counting qualify election support. Promotion resets progress and adds a current-term no-op. Higher-term messages normally relinquish authority; stale terms are rejected, with a recent-leader exception for higher-term vote requests. Configured quorum checks revoke inactive leadership. Transfer pauses proposals, waits for a full target to catch up and sends TimeoutNow; timeout cancels transfer. Reset drops volatile pending reads and votes while retaining log history. Application of removal revokes local leadership; restart restores persisted term/vote/commit and snapshot membership.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-authority\",\n        \"B-membership\",\n        \"B-recovery\",\n        \"B-persistence\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-pending-read\",\n        \"F-committed\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-formation\",\n        \"S-term\",\n        \"S-peer-admission\",\n        \"S-ticks\",\n        \"S-transfer\",\n        \"S-check-quorum\",\n        \"S-membership\",\n        \"S-recovery\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Only support qualified by current term/role and current membership advances formation; remote progress is rebuilt on authority reset while committed log history constrains future leaders through freshness and prefix checks. Pending configuration entries limit new proposals, and committed-but-unapplied work suppresses campaigning to avoid stale membership authority. RSM accepts legal configuration transitions then updates raft quorum membership. ReadIndex separately confirms current leadership only after current-term commitment, probes voting members and resolves a queued prefix; application and exact request context determine client completion. Old nonzero-term replies are filtered, pending read support is discarded on reset, and old log entries remain recoverable rather than being treated as current quorum proof.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-formation\",\n        \"B-authority\",\n        \"B-membership\",\n        \"B-read-admit\",\n        \"B-read-confirm\",\n        \"B-read-deliver\",\n        \"B-read-client\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-committed\",\n        \"F-pending-read\",\n        \"F-confirmed-read\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-term\",\n        \"S-formation\",\n        \"S-membership\",\n        \"S-rsm-config\",\n        \"S-read-consume\",\n        \"S-read-queue\",\n        \"S-read-response\",\n        \"S-client-batches\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"Remote confirmed-prefix response emission uses the triggering context for earlier remote requests; NodeHost client and application consequences remain outside the checked endpoint.\",\n      \"Pending confirmation support spanning membership changes requires an authority/timing history; local membership publication ordering is protected.\",\n      \"Result.Data ownership across session-history caching and client-visible responses is unresolved.\",\n      \"Logdb crash atomicity and on-disk application variants remain unread details.\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [],\n    \"status\": \"usable\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Representative formation and authority paths, their history/membership coupling and application boundaries are traced. Local questions and variants remain open; this is not coverage or correctness certification.\"\n  },\n  \"understanding_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"aa338cdddcde4dc586e05d7a64e169f2\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"aa338cdddcde4dc586e05d7a64e169f2\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"8c67f1f1b8f04030b7c320f25f45a4a2\",\n      \"version\": 2,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"8c67f1f1b8f04030b7c320f25f45a4a2\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"84f1a585f9104d09a1a20e57bd31b402\",\n      \"version\": 3,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"84f1a585f9104d09a1a20e57bd31b402\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"next_objective\": {\n    \"action\": \"investigate_and_refocus\",\n    \"boundary\": \"both_core_paths\",\n    \"reason\": \"Use results to update understanding and compare the remaining frontier\",\n    \"core_gaps\": []\n  },\n  \"drafts\": [],\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a118363ef443443ca4bcfe8f5be0f751\",\n      \"status\": \"paused\",\n      \"parent_candidate_id\": null,\n      \"fork_reason\": \"\",\n      \"obligation_id\": \"C-read-context\",\n      \"question_preview\": \"When a later heartbeat context confirms a prefix containing distinct remote read requests, does response propagation preserve the origin and context of each returned status, as required by exact-context completion at the requester?\",\n      \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n      \"result_claim_ids